      <h3>What soil types are common in Sydney pool excavation?</h3>
      <p>Sydney's soil varies significantly by suburb. Western Sydney typically has clay-heavy soil. The Northern Beaches and Eastern Suburbs often have sandstone requiring rock-breaking equipment. The Hills District has a mix of clay and shale. Always confirm soil conditions before booking your machine.</p>
